{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"99d19c13-4f53-45e1-be49-af4434dea423","runId":"6df31780-d744-4861-b63c-10444061fa07","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":13,"previousEventHash":"sha256:bc4c0887c300501807012ca80eff43d1c966516463887878d96e2b22e8b03778","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a043a0-1619-79aa-908b-82530636b6dd","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T14:31:59.755Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":["`src/adapters/github-projection.ts:479-480` rejects non-safe, non-positive issue numbers in `setWorkflowLabel` before delegation.","`src/adapters/github-projection.ts:525` calls `requireIssueNumber(issueNumber)` before constructing either issue API path, providing shared defense for receipt and clear variants.","`test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts` exercises valid workflow-label transitions but has no focused invalid-issue-number regression case.","Issue #209 records the original PR #199 review finding and expected regression coverage."],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Verdict | Invalid on current base |\n| Confidence | High |\n| Severity | Medium |\n| Task Type | Security regression coverage |\n\n### What Was Claimed\n\n`setWorkflowLabel` no longer validates `issueNumber` before interpolating it into GitHub API paths.\n\n### What We Found\n\nAt frozen base `6a8af2aaccf459b3ab45208032334e50a9ce629d`, `setWorkflowLabel` explicitly rejects non-safe and non-positive issue numbers. The shared `#replaceWorkflowLabel` helper also validates before constructing issue or label paths. The production defect is therefore not present, but focused regression coverage is missing.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe PR #199 review finding is stale relative to the current integration base. Existing code already enforces the invariant at both the public method and shared path-construction boundary; the remaining gap is test coverage.\n\n### Affected Files\n\n- `src/adapters/github-projection.ts` — existing validation boundary.\n- `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts` — missing malformed-input regression coverage.\n\n### Evidence\n\n- `setWorkflowLabel` checks `Number.isSafeInteger(issueNumber)` and positivity before delegation.\n- `#replaceWorkflowLabel` calls `requireIssueNumber(issueNumber)` before API path interpolation.\n- Existing adapter tests use only valid issue number `42` for workflow-label transitions.\n\n### History Findings\n\nIssue #209 originated from security finding `security-001` on PR #199 at reviewed head `a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3`. The frozen staging base now contains the missing guard; the supplied history does not identify the intervening commit.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nAdd one focused adapter regression test proving malformed issue numbers are rejected before transport access. Do not alter already-correct production behavior.\n\n### Related Issues\n\n- #209\n\n### Decomposition Assessment\n\nNo decomposition is required. The remaining work is a single focused test.\n\n### Acceptance Spec\n\n- [x] Validate the finding against the current integration branch.\n- [x] Confirm no production-code fix is required on the frozen base.\n- [ ] Add focused regression coverage.\n- [ ] Re-review the exact remediation head.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->","outputArtifactHash":"sha256:investigate-209-invalid-current-base"}}
